## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to handle real-world edge conditions where connectivity is unreliable, requiring robust reconciliation and canary control across regions.

## Key Concepts
- Edge buffering and eventual reconciliation
- Exactly-once ingestion with sequence numbers
- Per-tenant residency and regional logs
- Deterministic canary rollouts for feature flags
- Testing for outages, clock skew, and data loss

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent ingestion core
class IngestBuffer {
  constructor() { this.buffer = []; this.seen = new Set(); }
  enqueue(event) {
    const key = event.tenantId + ':' + event.seq;
    if (this.seen.has(key)) return;
    this.seen.add(key);
    this.buffer.push(event);
  }
  flush() { /* write to regional store; on failure keep in place for retry */ }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify reconciliation correctness under clock skew?
- How would you scale sequence-number state across millions of tenants?

## Why This Is Asked
Interview context explanation.

## Key Concepts
- Express routing
- Input validation and sanitization
- Parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection
- Error handling middleware
- Testing coverage (200/400/404)
- Response shaping and caching

## Code Example
```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const sqlite3 = require('sqlite3').verbose();
const db = new sqlite3.Database(':memory:');
app.get('/products', (req, res) => {
  db.all('SELECT id, name, price FROM products', [], (err, rows) => {
    if (err) return res.status(500).json({error:'db'});
    res.json(rows);
  });
});
app.get('/products/:id', (req, res) => {
  const id = parseInt(req.params.id, 10);
  if (Number.isNaN(id) || id <= 0) return res.status(400).json({error:'invalid_id'});
  db.get('SELECT id, name, price FROM products WHERE id = ?', [id], (err, row) => {
    if (err) return res.status(500).json({error:'db'});
    if (!row) return res.status(404).json({error:'not_found'});
    res.json(row);
  });
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you add pagination to /products?
- How do you test error paths (400/404/500) effectively?
